    "narrative": "Our highest-upside play today is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 80.77. Facing Quintana, a soft-tossing lefty with a 5.24 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** gains a massive 19% efficiency boost from the SP skill differential, and his position in the #2 hole ensures maximum RBI/R opportunities. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** (72.66) is an auto-start against Lugo; he is benefitting from a solid park factor and a favorable R/R platoon matchup that should allow him to exploit the middle of the order. **James Wood** (71.88) rounds out our top-tier tier; while we are waiting on official lineup confirmation, his projected leadoff spot against the struggling lefty P\u00e9rez makes him a high-efficiency engine for our run scoring today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision occurred at the fringe of the utility spots, where **Jose Caballero** (44.46) just missed the cut. While **Jose Caballero** remains an elite stash specifically for his stolen base upside, he was bumped by the superior efficiency scores of **Dalton Rushing** and **Cole Young**. The optimizer penalized **Jose Caballero** heavily for a dynamic platoon disadvantage and unfavorable wind conditions, which outweighed his potential to exploit the opposing starter's slow delivery. We are monitoring **James Wood** closely; should his lineup status shift, we may look to swap in **Henry Bolte** or **Kyle Karros**, though both remain below our current starting threshold for efficiency. \n\nWe are flagging **Brice Turang** for high-risk, as he faces a formidable arm in Yamamoto. While **Brice Turang** retains a solid score due to his high-leverage #2 spot in the order, his SP skill penalty (-17%) and the opponent's ability to control the running game (58% SB suppression) significantly cap his ceiling. **Vinnie Pasquantino** also warrants attention; although he maintains a strong score of 59.51, he is running into a pitcher in Woo who has a 3.42 xERA, meaning we are banking entirely on the platoon advantage to carry his output today. Keep a close eye on the weather and late-scratch potential for **James Wood** as we navigate a high-volume day.",
